  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="9ab608e9-deb6-5368-b4fa-359d2d5e5b9f" activityNameId="edbe9da0-2e7e-574e-8c9e-b1927c4664ca" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Process-specific burdens, municipal waste incineration</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Process-specific burdens, municipal waste incineration
Swiss municipal waste incineration plant with 100'000 ton per year capacity. Operational time 40 years;
Synonyms: MSWI, KVA; 
UUID: edab3419-2301-42b6-869a-5c9c606a2ff3
burdens in the municipal waste incineration process which are not attributable to a specific waste component, but are depending on operating conditions (temperature, oxygen concentrations etc.). Air emissions, burdens from emissions and abatement of thermal NOx, water consumption.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: average Swiss municipal soild waste incineration plants in 2000 with grate incinerator, with electrostatic precipitator for fly ash (ESP), wet flue gas scrubber and 29.4%  SNCR , 32.2%  SCR-high dust , 24.6%  SCR-low dust -DeNOx facilities and 13.8% without Denox  (by burnt waste, according to Swiss average).
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data from literature 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_edab3419-2301-42b6-869a-5c9c606a2ff3.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">CH</shortname>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Location: &lt;null&gt;</text>
        </comment>
      </geography>
      <technology>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Technology: average Swiss municipal soild waste incineration plants in 2000 with grate incinerator, with electrostatic precipitator for fly ash (ESP), wet flue gas scrubber and 29.4%  SNCR , 32.2%  SCR-high dust , 24.6%  SCR-low dust -DeNOx facilities and 13.8% without Denox  (by burnt waste, according to Swiss average).</text>
        </comment>
      </technology>
      <timePeriod startDate="2000-01-01" endDate="2000-12-31" isDataValidForEntirePeriod="true">
